  <section id="principles" class="principles-section" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <header class="section-header">
      <h2 id="principles-title">Rules the product actually enforces</h2>
      <p>Not testimonials. These are operating constraints a reviewer can verify in the product.</p>
    </header>
    <% rules = [
      ["Send rule", "A human reviews the current draft and presses Send. Agents cannot."],
      ["Ledger rule", "Tasks, runs, evidence, reviews, and sends stay attributable."],
      ["Memory rule", "Records carry source, time, scope, and supersession."],
      ["Runtime rule", "Rails submits work through the runner protocol. Go owns isolation."],
      ["Score rule", "Health signals stay inspectable. Analysis is labeled as analysis."],
      ["Degrade rule", "If memory or a runtime is down, NavishAI says so and keeps case work moving."],
      ["Policy rule", "Policy review surfaces missing evidence, stale sources, and conflicts before anyone can send."],
      ["Isolation rule", "Tenant, workspace, and memory scope stay isolated. PostgreSQL stays authoritative."],
      ["Channel rule", "Email and Intercom stay in the approved registry. No agent can send on either."]
    ] %>
    <div class="principle-stage" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="principle-columns">
        <% rules.each_slice(3).with_index do |group, index| %>
          <div class="principle-column principle-column-<%= index + 1 %>">
            <% 2.times do %>
              <div class="principle-column-track">
                <% group.each do |title, body| %>
                  <article class="principle-card">
                    <p><%= body %></p>
                    <footer>
                      <span class="principle-mark" aria-hidden="true"><%= title.first %></span>
                      <span>
                        <strong><%= title %></strong>
                        <small>Enforced in the product</small>
                      </span>
                    </footer>
                  </article>
                <% end %>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-fade principle-fade-top"></div>
      <div class="principle-fade principle-fade-bottom"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="principle-static">
      <% rules.each do |title, body| %>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <p><%= body %></p>
          <footer>
            <span class="principle-mark" aria-hidden="true"><%= title.first %></span>
            <span>
              <strong><%= title %></strong>
              <small>Enforced in the product</small>
            </span>
          </footer>
        </article>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq" class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <header class="section-header section-header-plain">
      <h2 id="faq-title">Questions before you install</h2>
      <p>Direct answers for operators reviewing a self-hosted workspace.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary>Who can send a customer message?</summary>
        <p>Only a signed-in human who reviews the current draft and presses Send in NavishAI. Agents, jobs, and earlier approvals cannot send later.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Does this replace Intercom on day one?</summary>
        <p>No. NavishAI can sit beside Intercom and shared email. Intercom remains authoritative for its native conversation. NavishAI owns crew work, evidence, memory, review, and the human-send audit.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Where do model credentials live?</summary>
        <p>Subscription CLI credentials stay on the customer-controlled runner. NavishAI does not import, copy, display, or store those login tokens.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What happens if memory is unavailable?</summary>
        <p>Authoritative writes and deterministic case work continue. Capture and recall stop in the open, with a warning. NavishAI does not fail over to a managed memory vendor.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is there a hosted trial or billed plan?</summary>
        <p>Not yet. Install the self-hosted product if you operate the stack. Billing stays manual until demand is validated.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Can we use our own scorecard?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Starting templates exist, but customer-specific scorecards are a core path: propose, preview, backtest, publish, and roll back a deterministic definition.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

